	(text "DDC I2C level shifted: 3.3 k pull-ups on the FPGA side, 4.7 k to +5 V on the cable side; EN tied to VREF2 through 200 k as the datasheet asks. +5 V to the monitor through a 500 mA polyfuse. HPD: the sink pulls it to +5 V, so 4.7 k in series and 10 k down put 3.2 V on the FPGA pin (the ECP5's limit is 3.6 V)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 308.61 148.59 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.85 0.85)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d924bae3-1497-8a24-d122-4f5a0b5110d6")
	)
	(text "microSD, 4-bit SD bus"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 379.73 232.41 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f0e673ae-bed7-4c87-f42d-7f5fd6e15d0e")
	)
	(text_box "The FT2232H gives two USB channels through one cable: channel A is the JTAG programmer (openFPGALoader -c ft2232), channel B is the serial console, so the console stays open while a bitstream loads and the whole boot can be captured. Its USB-C also powers the board (VBUS to the power sheet). The second USB-C goes straight to FPGA pins (ULX3S style) for soft USB devices: 27 Ω series, 15 kΩ\npull-downs, and a 1.5 kΩ pull-up on D+ switched by an FPGA pin. GPDI is the ULX3S/Icepi 22 nF-coupled HDMI; the DDC I2C is level shifted to 5 V. The microSD is wired 4-bit with pull-ups."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 25.4 0)
		(size 340.36 6.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3ac1ebd5-bc66-0674-a01f-78f4ea64e54a")
	)
